Pets attack monsters slightly stronger than them.  Most of the time
this strategy works because monsters only hit back in response.  If
the pet loses too many hit points it retreats and the monster pursues
you not your pet.

The problem with this strategy is there are a number of monsters that
hit very hard compared to their hit points.  I think giant mimics fit
this - hard hitting but easy to kill if you can survive their
attacks.  The
other problem is it does not take the monster's inventory into
account.
In the mine town the watch wears armor and wields weaons so they
are more dangerous compared to their level.  In particular the watch
captain wields 50-50 a long sword or silver saber.  Both are nice
enough
weapons classes that players tend to be wielding artifact versions of
them when they ascend.  Only a couple of hits from the watch captain
can kill a very buff pet.  I've lost plenty of pets to the watch
captain.

One strategy is to build a buff pet before getting to mine town but to
try to get to the monsters before your pet under mine town.  Try to
keep the pet weak enough on the way up that it won't attack the
watch captain (and priest and shopkeepers) or use polymorph to
get it strong enough that taking out those monsters is easy.



